BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: Modern Times — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261127T153000
DTSTAMP:20261126T082645Z
UID:e09d162498ca89a67ef32f2d41da@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:It starts with an overhead shot of sheep and cuts to the thron
 gs coming out of a subway station. Was Charlie Chaplin a Surrealist\, or j
 ust a realist? His version of modern times looks forward in equal measure 
 to Jacques Tati and 1984 . This “silent” is full of modern sounds\, he
 ard over loudspeakers and big corporate television screens (not to mention
  the Tramp’s outburst of French-inspired gibberish). Charlie\, the ever-
 elegant Tramp\, is an industrial swashbuckler with an oilcan for a sword\,
  but he’s begun taking on the characteristics of factory machines\, obse
 ssively twisting buttons no matter where they are.\nCategory: Films\nOrigi
 nal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331164-film-screenin
 g-modern-times
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
