BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Film Screening: The Last Waltz — Berkeley/San Francisco
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-08:00":20261127T173000
DTSTAMP:20261126T082645Z
UID:9dfb90bf81c06f5cb576962d69ee@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Films\,Berkeley/San Francisco\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Martin Scorsese grew up listening to seminal rock DJ Alan Free
 d\, and from Mean Streets onward\, his movies have been driven by the powe
 r of rock and roll. His love of music is innate and instinctual\, so when 
 The Band decided to hang it up after seventeen years on the road\, they ch
 ose Scorsese to film their farewell concert at Winterland Ballroom on Than
 ksgiving 1976. The film intercuts the glorious music from one of the all-t
 ime great concert lineups with interviews with members of The Band as they
  talk about their lives and music. The Last Waltz is an elegiac masterpiec
 e that captures a special moment in music history.\nCategory: Films\nOrigi
 nal listing: https://events.berkeley.edu/BAMPFA/event/331166-film-screenin
 g-the-last-waltz
LOCATION:BAMPFA\, BAMPFA
STATUS:CONFIRMED
