BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:National Symphony Orchestra: Handel's Messiah — Washington\, DC
DTSTART;TZID="UTC-05:00":20261216T190000
DTSTAMP:20261126T082645Z
UID:c4f14b8cb8c6d6f7ef269852c853@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Arts & Culture\,Washington\, DC\,United States
DESCRIPTION:Hallelujah! You know the chorus\, but there is a universe to d
 iscover beyond those famous four minutes. This December\, early-music mast
 er Richard Egarr makes his NSO debut conducting Handels Messiah\, the icon
 ic holiday favorite that can be hushed\, roaring\, and wondrously divine. 
 However you know Messiah as a yearly tradition\, a piece you sang yourself
 \, or music you have never heard live\, there is nothing like being in the
